@page "/demo-guide"

<PageTitle>Demo Guide - OperationsFlow</PageTitle>

<div class="of-page">
    <PageHero Eyebrow="OPERATIONSFLOW / DEMO"
              Title="Demo Guide"
              Subtitle="A clean walkthrough for showing OperationsFlow as a workflow, evidence, reporting, Microsoft 365, and role-based access pilot."
              BadgeText="Manager Review Ready"
              BadgeClass="of-badge of-badge-success">
        <Actions>
            <a class="of-btn of-btn-secondary" href="/reviewer-checklist">Reviewer Checklist</a>
            <a class="of-btn of-btn-secondary" href="/business-value">Business Value</a>
            <a class="of-btn of-btn-secondary" href="/technical-overview">Technical Overview</a>
            <a class="of-btn of-btn-primary" href="/dashboard">Dashboard</a>
        </Actions>
    </PageHero>

    <PurposeNote Title="Purpose" Icon="🎬">
        <p>
            This page gives a clean walkthrough for showing OperationsFlow to an employer, reviewer, or stakeholder.
            The demo should show that this is not just a dashboard: it has login, roles, workflow capture, supporting evidence,
            SharePoint storage, metadata writeback, quality checks, reports, and activity traceability.
        </p>
    </PurposeNote>

    <TableCard Title="Demo accounts"
               Subtitle="Use local SQL accounts for quick role testing. Microsoft sign-in can be used to prove tenant identity linking.">
        <ChildContent>
            <table class="table">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th>Role</th>
                        <th>Username</th>
                        <th>Password</th>
                        <th>What to show</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr>
                        <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-danger">Admin</span></td>
                        <td>admin</td>
                        <td>Admin123!</td>
                        <td>Full access, user roles, settings, evidence, reports, Microsoft/SharePoint config, and logout.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-warning">Manager</span></td>
                        <td>manager</td>
                        <td>Manager123!</td>
                        <td>Operational oversight, workflow records, reports, exports, and data quality.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-info">Reviewer</span></td>
                        <td>reviewer</td>
                        <td>Reviewer123!</td>
                        <td>Evidence, document library, reports, activity, and audit-style review.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-success">Worker</span></td>
                        <td>worker</td>
                        <td>Worker123!</td>
                        <td>Assigned work and evidence upload path.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-muted">ReadOnly</span></td>
                        <td>viewer</td>
                        <td>Viewer123!</td>
                        <td>View-only stakeholder path with no upload/delete/export actions.</td>
                    </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </ChildContent>
    </TableCard>

    <InfoPanel Title="Recommended demo flow"
               Subtitle="Use this order to show the project clearly.">
        <ChildContent>
            <div class="of-review-proof-grid">
                <div class="of-review-proof-card">
                    <span class="of-badge of-badge-info">Step 1</span>
                    <h3>Start at login</h3>
                    <p>
                        Open the app at /login. Show both local login and Microsoft sign-in.
                        Explain that Microsoft sign-in maps a tenant account to a local OperationsFlow role.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="of-review-proof-card">
                    <span class="of-badge of-badge-info">Step 2</span>
                    <h3>Show local vs Microsoft status</h3>
                    <p>
                        Sign in locally and show the Local login badge. Then sign in with Microsoft and show the Microsoft-linked badge.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="of-review-proof-card">
                    <span class="of-badge of-badge-info">Step 3</span>
                    <h3>Dashboard overview</h3>
                    <p>
                        Show operational volume: work orders, corrective actions, document reviews, risks, training, and document intake.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="of-review-proof-card">
                    <span class="of-badge of-badge-info">Step 4</span>
                    <h3>User roles</h3>
                    <p>
                        Open User Roles and show local SQL users, role matrix, permissions, and Microsoft external login links.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="of-review-proof-card">
                    <span class="of-badge of-badge-info">Step 5</span>
                    <h3>Admin Settings</h3>
                    <p>
                        Run the Microsoft 365 connection test and show Graph, SharePoint site, and document library resolution.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="of-review-proof-card">
                    <span class="of-badge of-badge-info">Step 6</span>
                    <h3>Record details + evidence</h3>
                    <p>
                        Open a Work Order detail page and upload evidence. Show the file landing in SharePoint under the record folder.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="of-review-proof-card">
                    <span class="of-badge of-badge-info">Step 7</span>
                    <h3>SharePoint metadata</h3>
                    <p>
                        Open the SharePoint file and show OperationsFlowModule, RecordId, RecordRef, evidence flag, uploader, and notes.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="of-review-proof-card">
                    <span class="of-badge of-badge-info">Step 8</span>
                    <h3>Document Library</h3>
                    <p>
                        Show central SharePoint-backed evidence records with provider, module, type, open link, and delete lifecycle.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="of-review-proof-card">
                    <span class="of-badge of-badge-info">Step 9</span>
                    <h3>Activity Log</h3>
                    <p>
                        Show upload/delete events and confirm the current user is recorded instead of a generic demo user.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="of-review-proof-card">
                    <span class="of-badge of-badge-info">Step 10</span>
                    <h3>ReadOnly check</h3>
                    <p>
                        Sign in as ReadOnly and show that upload, delete, edit, and export actions are hidden/blocked.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </ChildContent>
    </InfoPanel>

    <TableCard Title="What the demo proves"
               Subtitle="Use these points when explaining the project.">
        <ChildContent>
            <table class="table">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th>Area</th>
                        <th>Proof</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr>
                        <td>Authentication</td>
                        <td>Local SQL login and Microsoft OAuth2 sign-in both work.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>Authorization</td>
                        <td>Local SQL roles and permissions control app behaviour.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>Microsoft linking</td>
                        <td>Microsoft tenant accounts map to LocalUser through ExternalLoginLinks.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>Storage</td>
                        <td>Evidence files upload to SharePoint through Microsoft Graph.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>Metadata</td>
                        <td>OperationsFlow writes module, record, evidence, uploader, and notes metadata to SharePoint columns.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>Traceability</td>
                        <td>Activity Log records workflow and file lifecycle events.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>Reviewability</td>
                        <td>Reports and Data Quality pages make missing evidence and review gaps visible.</td>
                    </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </ChildContent>
    </TableCard>

    <GuidanceNote Title="How to present it" Icon="✅" Tone="success">
        <p>
            Present OperationsFlow as a production pilot-ready Microsoft 365 workflow system, not a finished enterprise SaaS platform.
            The honest positioning is: local production foundation plus working single-tenant Microsoft 365 pilot integration.
        </p>
    </GuidanceNote>
</div>